<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Python on Tech and Lifestyle Blog</title><link>https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/tags/python/</link><description>Recent content in Python on Tech and Lifestyle Blog</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><copyright>© 2025 Yalchin Mammadli</copyright><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 May 2025 21:43:57 +0200</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/tags/python/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Sorting Algorithms and Binary Search in Python</title><link>https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/sorting-algorithms-and-binary-search-in-python/</link><pubDate>Fri, 16 May 2025 21:43:57 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/sorting-algorithms-and-binary-search-in-python/</guid><description>&lt;h2 class="relative group">&lt;strong>Selection Sort&lt;/strong>
&lt;div id="selection-sort" class="anchor">&lt;/div>
&lt;span
class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none">
&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#selection-sort" aria-label="Anchor">#&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Selection sort is about selecting the minimum value in an unsorted array and moving it towards the front by comparing. Here is an example code snippet to implement binary search in Python:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-py" data-lang="py">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="k">def&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nf">selection_sort&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">list_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">):&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">length&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nb">len&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">list_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">for&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">index&lt;/span> &lt;span class="ow">in&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nb">range&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">length&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">-&lt;/span> &lt;span class="mi">1&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">):&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="nb">min&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">list_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">index&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">]&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">for&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">j&lt;/span> &lt;span class="ow">in&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nb">range&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">index&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">+&lt;/span> &lt;span class="mi">1&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">length&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">):&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">if&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">list_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">j&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">]&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">&amp;lt;&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nb">min&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="nb">min&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">list_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">j&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">]&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">list_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">j&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">],&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">list_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">index&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">]&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">list_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">index&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">],&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">list_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">j&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">]&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">return&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">list_&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="n">unsorted_list&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="p">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">7&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">8&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">9&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">8&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">7&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">6&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">5&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">6&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">7&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">8&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">9&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">8&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">7&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">6&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">5&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">6&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">7&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">8&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">0&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">]&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="n">selection_sort&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">unsorted_list&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>
&lt;h3 class="relative group">&lt;strong>Buble Sort&lt;/strong>
&lt;div id="buble-sort" class="anchor">&lt;/div>
&lt;span
class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none">
&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#buble-sort" aria-label="Anchor">#&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h3>
&lt;p>The bubble sort algorithm is applied by going through an array of data a number of times and at the same time comparing two adjacent numbers at a time in order to reorder them if there are out of order. Here is an example snippet written in Python:&lt;/p></description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/sorting-algorithms-and-binary-search-in-python/featured.png"/></item><item><title>Map Sort Filter Functions in Python</title><link>https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/map-sort-filter-functions-in-python/</link><pubDate>Fri, 16 May 2025 21:28:34 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/map-sort-filter-functions-in-python/</guid><description>&lt;p>This tutorial will help you to see real example of using map, sort, and filter functions along with lambda functions in Python.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>&lt;strong>Map Function Example&lt;/strong>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Python&amp;rsquo;s map() is a built-in function that allows you to process and transform all the items in an iterable without using an explicit for loop, a technique commonly known as mapping. map() is useful when you need to apply a transformation function to each item in an iterable and transform them into a new iterable.&lt;/p></description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/map-sort-filter-functions-in-python/featured.png"/></item><item><title>Python Decorators With Function and Decorator Parameters</title><link>https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/python-decorators-with-function-and-decorator-parameters/</link><pubDate>Fri, 16 May 2025 21:17:13 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/python-decorators-with-function-and-decorator-parameters/</guid><description>&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-py" data-lang="py">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="k">def&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nf">modify_multiply_decorator&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">*&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">args&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">**&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">kwargs&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">):&lt;/span> &lt;span class="c1"># coeff=3&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">def&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nf">dec&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">multiply_func&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">):&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">def&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nf">inner&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">*&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">nums&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">):&lt;/span> &lt;span class="c1"># (2, 290)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">coefficient&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">kwargs&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="s2">&amp;#34;coefficient&amp;#34;&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">]&lt;/span> &lt;span class="c1"># 3&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">result&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">multiply_func&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">*&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">nums&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">)&lt;/span> &lt;span class="c1"># 2 * 290&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">modified_result&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">coefficient&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">*&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">result&lt;/span> &lt;span class="c1"># 3 * 580&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">return&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">modified_result&lt;/span> &lt;span class="c1"># 1740&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">return&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">inner&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">return&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">dec&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-py" data-lang="py">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="nd">@modify_multiply_decorator&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">coefficient&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">=&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">3&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="k">def&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nf">multiply&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">*&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">nums&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">):&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">return&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">nums&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">0&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">]&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">*&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">nums&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">1&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">]&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="nb">print&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">multiply&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">2&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">290&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">))&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div></description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/python-decorators-with-function-and-decorator-parameters/featured.png"/></item><item><title>How to Setup Mailgun in Django</title><link>https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/how-to-setup-mailgun-in-django/</link><pubDate>Thu, 15 May 2025 12:29:36 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/how-to-setup-mailgun-in-django/</guid><description>&lt;p>In this tutorial, I will try to cover configuring a custom domain for sending emails in your application. The benefit of using mailgun is that it allows you to send (5,000) emails for free during the first three months (then you will pay $0.8 per 1,000 emails) and its setup procedure is so straightforward. You will only need to add your payment verification to be able to send emails without any restrictions.&lt;/p></description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/how-to-setup-mailgun-in-django/featured.png"/></item><item><title>Accent and Case Insensitive Search and Minimum Distance Calculator in Pymongo</title><link>https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/accent-and-case-sensitive-search-pymongo/</link><pubDate>Tue, 13 May 2025 00:51:03 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/accent-and-case-sensitive-search-pymongo/</guid><description>&lt;h1 class="relative group">Ellaborate case
&lt;div id="ellaborate-case" class="anchor">&lt;/div>
&lt;span
class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none">
&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#ellaborate-case" aria-label="Anchor">#&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h1>
&lt;p>Before starting with set up and everything, I would love to confess that I find Mongodb and Python combination as &lt;strong>pain in the ass&lt;/strong>. Recently I have got an job offer as Python/Flask developer in one of the local companies in my country. They are using Mongodb as their production database. They requested a little bit of task to accomplish before we move on to HR interview. So the task was about coding autocomplete search logic and also finding the closest location to our current location from the database. Task seems interesting and pretty much easy to solve, at least for me as a Django developer who have used Postgresql as default database in most of the cases. However, seemed like things don&amp;rsquo;t go so well with Mongodb in django. It seemed like if Python is envolved, we normally have two pypi packages two use, namely &lt;a
href="https://pymongo.readthedocs.io/en/stable/"
target="_blank"
>pymongo&lt;/a> and &lt;a
href="https://docs.mongoengine.org/"
target="_blank"
>mongoengine&lt;/a>. I was familiar with pymongo as in my &lt;a
href="https://t.me/mp3converteryoutubebot"
target="_blank"
>telegram bot&lt;/a> I use Mongodb as database and use pymongo to implement database actions. Hence, below I will explain how I implemented case and accent insensitive search and minimum distance finding via pymongo.&lt;/p></description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/accent-and-case-sensitive-search-pymongo/featured.png"/></item></channel></rss>